# ============================================================================
# 04_ Multi-task elastic net: NEPC_score + ASPC_fraction — v3
# ============================================================================
# Consumes 02_ and 03_; writes the coefficient / stability tables 06_ reads.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE ERROR THAT MOTIVATED v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Error in ... 'select' for signature 'x = "tbl_df"'
#
# `select` resolved to AnnotationDbi::select(), not dplyr::select(). edgeR
# attaches AnnotationDbi transitively, and because it loads AFTER dplyr in the
# suppressPackageStartupMessages block it wins the search path. AnnotationDbi's
# select() is an S4 generic with no tbl_df method, hence "unable to find an
# inherited method".
#
# This is the same class of bug that hit 06_ v4 (MASS::select via WGCNA). The
# durable fix is not load order — that breaks again the moment a dependency
# changes — but namespace qualification. Every dplyr verb in v3 is written
# dplyr::verb(), and stats::sd / stats::var / stats::median are qualified too.
#
# The v2 run reached Step 8 and WROTE ALL THREE CSVs before failing. Only the
# final console print died. So multi_task_coefficients.csv and
# stability_selection.csv on disk are valid — v3 changes no numerical result,
# it just lets the script finish and adds the diagnostics below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE v2 RUN PRODUCED, AND THE PROBLEM IT REVEALS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   NEPC_score    alpha 0.3  lambda 0.172  CV err 0.106  80 non-zero of 3402
#   ASPC_fraction alpha 0.5  lambda 0.203  CV err 0.317  31 non-zero of 3402
#   213 samples, 3402 features, feature_source = single_cell
#
# 06_ v8 then reported e_stab = 0 of 418 and e_mtl = 0 of 418 — both ML
# channels contributed nothing to every gene. With 80 and 31 non-zero
# coefficients from disjoint fits, the overlap positive in BOTH is plausibly
# empty, and bootstrap frequencies rarely clear a cutoff. v3 therefore REPORTS
# the joint counts and the stability distribution explicitly instead of leaving
# 06_ to discover the channels are inert.
#
# Do not lower cfg$stability_cutoff to manufacture hits. If nothing is stable,
# that is the finding: with p/n = 16 the coefficients are not reproducible.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OTHER CHANGES IN v3
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   * `%||%` moved above first use (it worked by luck of evaluation order).
#   * `feat_tbl$source` set before the fallback branch can reference it.
#   * stability_freq_min computed with an explicit pmin guard; the previous
#     pmin(a, b, na.rm = TRUE) returns the non-NA value when one side is NA,
#     which silently overstates joint stability.
#   * Correlation between the two targets reported BEFORE fitting. If
#     NEPC_score and ASPC_fraction are uncorrelated, multi_task_positive is
#     near-empty by construction and 06_'s channel cannot fire.
#   * Final summary block wrapped so a printing failure cannot mask a
#     successful run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A LIMIT THAT GOVERNS INTERPRETATION
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEPC_score is computed from logCPM — the same matrix supplying the
# predictors. Regressing genes on a score built from other genes in the same
# samples finds structure regardless of the biology. coef_NEPC_like is a
# consistency check, not prediction, and 06_ should weight it lowest. If
# pathology labels exist, use them instead.
#
# OUTPUTS (out_dir)
#   multi_task_coefficients.csv   gene, coef_NEPC_like, coef_ASPC_fraction,
#                                 multi_task_positive          <- 06_ reads
#   stability_selection.csv       gene, stability_freq, stability_freq_aspc,
#                                 stability_selected           <- 06_ reads
#   aspc_features_bulk.csv        feature universe + provenance
#   model_diagnostics.csv         per-target alpha, lambda, CV error, n_nonzero
#   nepc_score_per_sample.csv     computed scores, for inspection
#   04_PROVENANCE.txt
# ============================================================================

